{
  "fixtureVersion": 1,
  "id": "read-update-sequence-idempotency-dispositions",
  "description": "The three idempotency-key dispositions as sequence-member problems: a retained key presented with different semantics (conflict), a key whose first member is still in flight (in-progress, then the retained disposition on retry), and a key whose retained outcome was discarded after the retention interval (expired). Runs after read-update-sequence-idempotent-retry: w1-note-create is retained. Illustrative wire example; not evidence.",
